(1931395, 262795, 27735, '<td valign="top">There really wasn''t much wind. I think smoke came out of the large stack with much greater force than the other stacks, causing the smoke to go straight up. Smoke from the other stacks seemed like it just floated around.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by theSaj:</b></div><hr/><i> Okay, how the heck did you get the smoke on the left to bellow inward, the smoke on the right to also bellow inward. And the center stack to bellow it''s smoke straight up!!!!<br/> <br/>That''s like near impossible without a cyclone....*lol* </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'There really wasn''t much wind. I think smoke came out of the large stack with much greater force than the other stacks, causing the smoke to go straight up. Smoke from the other stacks seemed like it just floated around. Originally posted by theSaj: Okay, how the heck did you get the smoke on the left to bellow inward, the smoke on the right to also bellow inward. And the center stack to bellow it''s smoke straight up!!!! That''s like near impossible without a cyclone....*lol* ', '2005-12-07 11:10:59.000000', NULL, 0),
